{ns}
{define: CaddG base-fret 1 frets x 3 2 0 1 3} 
{define: D# base-fret 1 frets x x 5 3 4 3}
{define: Dsus4 base-fret 1 frets x x 0 2 3 3}
{define: Em/G base-fret 1 frets 0 2 2 0 0 3}  
{define: F base-fret 1 frets x x 3 2 1 1}
{define: Gadd base-fret 1 frets 3 2 0 0 3 3} 
{t: WHEN YOU’RE NEXT TO ME (In G) – Mitch & Mickey }
{st: (Levy) }
{artist: Mitch & Mickey }
{composer: Eugene Levy }


https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=a4sVu0z5Qo8  (Capo 7) (MC5)

TIP:  If transposing, play the root chord of the (CaddG), (Em/G), and (Gadd) adding the 5th note as necessary.

TIP:  To play the (CaddG), (Em/G), and (D4) just add the pinky to the 1st string/3rd fret when playing the (C), (Em) and (D).   

TIP:  The (D#) is (D) up one fret but you need to add the pinky to the 4th string/4th fret.  And do not strike the top two strings.
 
TIP:  The |D| in brackets means to strum once and sustain until the following (G).  And if the rapid (C)(G) chord changes between the (G) and (D) are too much, just play the (G) straight through to the first (D).   
       

